  <h2>What Is an Audio Visualizer?</h2>

  <p>
    An Audio Visualizer converts sound into a real-time animation: bars, waveforms, or circles that move to the music. The result is an animated MP4 video that "dances" to your track — ideal for:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>Music releases</strong> on TikTok, Instagram Reels and YouTube Shorts</li>
    <li><strong>Podcast clips</strong> with higher engagement than static images</li>
    <li><strong>Waveform videos</strong> for SoundCloud promotions</li>
    <li><strong>Relaxation music</strong>, ambient tracks and meditation content</li>
    <li><strong>Music previews</strong> before the official release</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Step-by-Step: Create a TikTok Music Video with the Audio Visualizer</h2>

  <ol class="steps">
    <li>
      <div class="step-content">
        <strong>Open the Audio Visualizer</strong>
        <p>Visit <a href="https://kodinitools.com/visualizer/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kodinitools.com/visualizer</a> — no download, no account.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="step-content">
        <strong>Upload your audio file</strong>
        <p>Supports MP3, WAV, OGG and M4A. The file stays locally on your device.</p>
